DarthBob88 wrote:
> John Richert wrote:
> > If an artifact is hit with a wand of Cancellation, is it still an artifact
> > or does it become its normal type, i.e. if Excalibur is hit by the wand does
> > it become a long sword, or is it just a uncursed Excalibur?
>
> AFAIK, a cancelled artifact becomes uncursed and +0 artifact. This is
> most useful when trying to get a +7 Mojo and similar.

This is correct. Once an artifact, always an artifact. This is true
even for artifacts created by #naming. Interestingly enough, though,
wizmode testing reveals that corrosion/rusting/rotting/fooproofing
remains intact. If you somehow wind up with the blessed +0 thoroughly
rusted Mjollnir, cancellation isn't the answer.

Furthermore, I'm about 95% sure that a destroyed artifact still counts
against you when wishing for new artifacts. The odds for artifact
wishing depend only on the number of artifacts *created* in the game,
regardless of whether they still exist. In other words, eating
Ogresmasher won't help you get your wish for Frostbrand (or whatever
suits your fancy).



